- add-holds-axiom after cynder_not_good gives 'axiom cynder_not_good.holds : cynder_not_good';
- holds-theorem-to-axiom archives exactly the theorem's text;
- remove-holds and remove-decl remove the docstring and the spacing;
- add-hypothesis on 'theorem d1.holds (h : cynder_not_good) : d1 := ...' gives 'theorem d1.holds (h_x : x) (h : cynder_not_good) : d1 := ...' and replaces the given spans;
- apply-hypothesis wraps c as (c h_x) and @c as (@c h_x);
- set-docstring inserts and replaces, escaping both comment delimiters;
- a missing declaration is reported in problems and no edits are returned

AT2.2 One test per cell of the 6.3 status table (ASSUMPTION/DERIVATION/GOAL x H absent/axiom/theorem/theorem with sorryAx), plus:
- conditional vs proved from a wrapped #check type;
- holds-mismatch;
- justificationKind other;
- footprint mapping including presup: and axiom: entries with TL103;
- rests-on-claimed;
- self-evident;
- existence-commitment with TL108;
- TL102;
- a block bound to a theorem or to a bare axiom is ill-formed with TL113;
- a Lean error inside one node's .holds makes only that node ill-formed

AT2.3 Stale and unchecked files:
- a stale file keeps its previous facts by name while the keyword is unchanged (stale flag, no refs, uses kept);
