- nodes of failed, dependency-failed and not-built modules get not-checked

AT2.4 uses and refs come from DeclFacts.refs and are never hard-coded:
- changing the fixture's refs changes uses;
- the closure runs through another node's statement and through a vocabulary definition;
- refs are code-relative, include the card's own statement inside its .holds, and drop non-vocabulary refs (e.g. And.right, Nat);
- for the Spyro fixture, every ref's substring is a suffix of its name

AT2.5 Vocabulary classification per 6.4 with typeSort:
