 70	/**
 71	 * The texts telelean just wrote to each file (null = deleted), in order, for a few seconds: an event whose text
 72	 * equals one of them is an echo of telelean's own write.
 73	 *
 74	 * Each stream observes telelean's writes to a file in order, but an event can be handled late: when telelean writes
 75	 * a file twice in quick succession (an action and its Undo), the file event of the first write may be handled after
 76	 * the second write was recorded, and still read the first text from disk. So an event may match any text recorded
 77	 * since the one its stream matched last (the oldest such match is taken, so a later event can still match a newer
 78	 * one), not only the latest. An event with any other text (the user typed, another program wrote the file) forgets
 79	 * every text recorded so far for its stream, so that a later return to one of them (Undo in the editor) is not
 80	 * mistaken for an echo.
